 "result_text": "I fixed the ordering bug in `nose2/suite.py`. I didn't run the gist's example, so I haven't confirmed the fix on a case like yours, and I didn't add a test for it.\n\n**Cause:** When the layers plugin sorts tests, regular `unittest` tests stay in a plain top-level suite. A plain suite only runs `tearDownClass` for the last regular test class once the whole run is finishing. By then the layer suites, which sit inside that same suite, have already run. That is why layer `setUp` calls ended up between a class's `setUpClass` and its `tearDownClass`.\n\n**Fix:** `LayerSuite.run` now tears down any pending class and module fixtures from preceding non-layer tests before it sets up its own layer. The new method is `handle_previous_test_teardown`.\n\n**Tests:** The functional and unit suites show the same failures with and without my change: 1 and 9 failures. I didn't look into why they fail.",
